# twin_mode7_lid_slstm.config -- Phase 9 Task 5 LID mechanical-wiring fixture, Mode 7 (spec S8.3).
# GENERATED by scripts/extract_phase9_fixtures.py from the committed phase-4b
# twin_train.config: SAME phSeq corpus, SAME frozen SAD net, LID net swapped to the
# phase-9 sLSTM cell. Epochs forced to 0 so run() is a single fold at theta (F11).
# twin_train.config -- Phase 4b Task 9 (TwinBlstmSpectralLid / Algo 6, Mode 7, TRAIN).
# twin_mode7.config with TINY nets (every GEMM reduction dim < 23, so the REAL compiled
# Eigen engine and the ascending-loop port agree bit-for-bit on the oracle machine --
# the manifest's nn_product_probes boundary), BLSTM_LID_BackPropagationActivated true,
# 3 training epochs, and a 2-file phSeq corpus WITH .stm references (scored -m mode).
# Both nets are seeded from committed synthFlat .bin files (workdir-relative), the
# single source of truth for the harness AND the Rust replay.
# RpropInit 0.15 / 6 epochs: MEASURED fire+skip best-cost trajectory on the algo-6
# cost+costLID criterion (fired=5 skipped=2; costLID rises at epochs 5/7 -- see
# manifest.json:corpus_lid.measured.train.twin_train). Smaller inits/fewer epochs
# descend monotonically (gate never skips) and the ns/nsx gate pin never diverges.
